.TH "PKGEXEC_RESULT_CODEC" "3" "" "libpkgexec" "Version 2.1.0"
.SH NAME
pkgexec_result_codec \- durable native execution\-result evidence encoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]#include <libpkgexec/result_codec.h>\f[R]
.IP
.EX
execution_result_encoding encode_execution_result(
    const execution_result& result);

execution_result decode_execution_result(
    const execution_result_encoding& encoding,
    execution_request request,
    backend_capability_profile backend);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The execution\-result codec retains the observation fields owned by \f[B]libpkgexec\f[R]: process\-start state, interpreter observation, termination, stream evidence, established guarantees, cleanup, typed failure, diagnostic text, and the sealed evidence identity.
.PP
The semantic execution request and backend capability profile are not serialized or reconstructed from identities.
Their exact identities are stored in the record, and the caller must supply both complete authorities to \f[B]decode_execution_result\f[R].
.PP
Decoding verifies the record checksum before interpreting authority fields, requires the supplied request and backend profile identities, reconstructs the result through the ordinary invariant\-enforcing factories, recomputes the execution\-evidence identity, and requires canonical re\-encoding.
.PP
Cancellation evidence is reconstructed with a fresh request\-bound \f[B]cancellation_source\f[R] whose signal is transitioned before the cancellation factory is called.
The operational cancellation state is not retained as semantic identity.
.PP
Diagnostic text remains outside execution\-evidence identity, but it is covered by the durable record checksum.
Altering a diagnostic therefore corrupts the record even though it does not change semantic result identity.
.SH LIMITS
One encoding is limited by \f[B]maximum_execution_result_encoding_size\f[R].
Diagnostic and retained stream material fields have bounded lengths.
Oversized, truncated, noncanonical, checksum\-invalid, or semantically impossible encodings are rejected with \f[B]error_code::corrupt_encoding\f[R].
.PP
Supplying another request or backend profile is rejected with \f[B]error_code::authority_mismatch\f[R].
.SH BOUNDARY
The codec does not serialize source programs, execution requests, backend profiles, host resource paths, cancellation state, build results, check results, lifecycle results, or controller sessions.
It is a subordinate evidence codec, not an execution\-session archive or recovery policy.
